# .maroonignore — paths Maroon Elephant skips when scanning THIS repo.
# Glob patterns, gitignore-ish. A directory excludes everything under it.

# Intentionally-vulnerable test fixtures and the test corpus are not product source
# (they deliberately contain the patterns the scanner looks for).
benchmarks/fixtures
tests

# Prose research/spec docs and generated site/docs (not code under analysis).
Findings.md
Build Plan.md
site
docs

# Detection-pattern & knowledge definitions. These files ENUMERATE the very attack
# patterns/keywords the scanner looks for, so pattern-based rules match them by
# construction (the classic "scanning the scanner" false positive). Excluding them is
# standard practice (cf. Semgrep's .semgrepignore). The real attack surface of Maroon
# Elephant — ingest, engine, model, cli, reporters, ui, github, mcpserver — IS scanned.
maroon/knowledge
maroon/analyzer.py
maroon/taint.py
maroon/detect.py
